Prevent pipe deadlocks during initial pod pushes

Git cat-file can fill its response pipe while LFS preparation is still
writing object IDs, leaving pod setup and its lifecycle lock stuck.
Write requests in a scoped thread while draining stdout and stderr, and
join the writer before returning so write errors remain visible.

Report the initial branch push separately from submodule setup,
including slow-operation progress. Exercise initial entry and reentry
with 32768 image-only commits so the non-LFS regression exceeds pipe
capacity and verifies that the full branch history reaches the host.
